### Section 2: Architecture & Node Walkthrough (0:35 – 2:00)

**[Action: Zoom in on the n8n Canvas and highlight each node as you speak]**

> *"Let’s look at the system architecture."*
>
> **1. Webhook Ingress:**  
> *"First, we have an HTTP Webhook trigger. It acts as an asynchronous entry point for inbound form submissions, instantly returning a 200 OK response to prevent web form timeouts."*
>
> **2. NVIDIA NIM AI Call:**  
> *"Next, the payload is sent to NVIDIA’s NIM API running `meta/llama-3.1-70b-instruct`. Instead of locked-in proprietary models like OpenAI or Claude, using NVIDIA NIM gives us open-source privacy compliance, zero data retention, and lower latency. We enforce a system prompt that mandates strict JSON output and run the model at a low temperature of 0.1 for deterministic classification."*
>
> **3. Defensive JavaScript Code Parser:**  
> *"Node 3 is one of the most critical engineering steps: our Code Parser. LLMs are non-deterministic and can output markdown tags or invisible control characters that crash standard `JSON.parse()` calls. In this node, I wrote a multi-layered defense mechanism that strips markdown fences, removes ASCII control characters, applies regex fallback extraction, and performs strict type coercion on the `route_to_human` boolean. I also added a keyword override safeguard to catch critical terms like 'outage' or 'system down'."*
>
> **4. Decision Engine (IF Branch):**  
> *"Node 4 evaluates `route_to_human`. To prevent type-mismatch bugs where a string `"true"` fails a strict boolean check, the condition sanitizes and casts the value before evaluating."*
>
> **5. Salesforce REST API Write Nodes:**  
> *"Finally, Nodes 5 and 6 connect to Salesforce’s SObjects REST API using OAuth2 authentication via a Salesforce Connected App. Depending on the branch, it creates a Lead record with mapped fields and embeds the AI's full diagnostic reasoning—summary, pain point, and confidence score—directly into the Lead Description."*

